 or down.\n    The path length is constant (2*N - 1), so maximizing the average is equivalent to maximizing the sum.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not matrix or not matrix[0]:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input matrix must be non-empty and square.\")\n\n    n = len(matrix)\n    # Validate squareness\n    for row in matrix:\n        if len(row) != n:\n            raise ValueError(\"Input matrix must be square (n x n).\")\n\n    # dp[r][c] stores the maximum sum obtainable from (0, 0) to (r, c).\n    dp = [[0.0] * n for _ in range(n)]\n\n    # Initialize the top-left cell.\n    dp[0][0] = float(matrix[0][0])\n\n    # Fill the first row (only move right)\n    for c in range(1, n):\n        dp[0][c] = dp[0][c - 1] + float(matrix[0][c])\n\n    # Fill the first column (only move down)\n    for r in range(1, n):\n        dp[r][0] = dp[r - 1][0] + float(matrix[r][0])\n\n    # Fill the rest of the dp table\n    for r in range(1, n):\n        for c in range(1, n):\n            # Choose the path (from above or left) that yields the maximum sum\n            if dp[r - 1][c] > dp[r][c - 1]:\n                dp[r][c] = dp[r - 1][c] + float(matrix[r][c])\n            else:\n                dp[r][c] = dp[r][c - 1] + float(matrix[r][c])\n\n    # The maximum total sum is at the bottom-right cell\n    total_sum = dp[n - 1][n - 1]\n\n    # The path length for any valid path in an N*N matrix is fixed at 2*N - 1\n    path_length = 2 * n - 1\n\n    return total_sum / path_length", "base_status": "pass", "plus_status": "pass", "base_fail_tests": [], "plus_fail_tests": []}], "Mbpp/726": [{"task_id": "Mbpp/726", "solution": "from typing import Tuple, Union\ndef multiply_elements(items: Tuple[Union[int, float], ...]) -> Tuple[Union[int, float], ...]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the product of adjacent elements in a tuple of numbers.\n    Returns a new tuple where each element is the product of adjacent input elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    results = []\n    for a, b in zip(items, items[1:]):\n        results.ap